From 06d6549f8dabc4766aeaf4a24d7d2167d0bf8a34 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: RDoom <171243930+aeon1911@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 20:13:03 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 37/55] Switch Vulkan: preload the effect textures a game used,
 dynres from frame pacing

Console logs (87e335d13): the first explosion still dropped frames even
in a second session, because every fire/smoke/gore sprite was uploaded the
first time it appeared (9-23 textures per frame); the second explosion
was smooth. And the dynamic resolution stayed at 60%: with the scene
submitted early, the GPU timestamps of a frame include the idle gaps
between its submits.

- Untranslated sprites, skin sprites and decals first drawn during a level
  are listed per game (cache/uzdoom/rdoom-textures-<hash>.txt) and
  uploaded at the end of the next level precache (PrecacheUsedTextures).
- The dynamic resolution now drops only when the previous frame missed
  vsync and this one had to wait for the GPU, and climbs back by 10% after
  45 frames on time without waiting.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
